      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BETTOR THAN READY (1) scored again to make it three wins in succession at his latest appearance over 1609m at this track, getting home by 1.3 metres after taking charge a fair way out. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Beautifully placed and is sure to prove tough to beat. POGACAR (4) won at this track two runs ago but couldn't repeat the dose at his latest appearance over 1680m at Launceston, beaten 4 metres. This is a nice drop in grade so he is a major player. OUR ROB ROY (3) should be at his peak for this. Finished third over 1680m at Launceston at the latest appearance a week-and-a-half ago. Sure to give the top fancies plenty to think about. MYSTERY MAIL (6) must be considered after he finished runner-up when resuming over 1609m at this track five days ago.",
